411:\section{Introduction}
413:We study a natural periodic scheduling problem faced by groups of regularity-loving polyamorous people:
414:Consider a set of persons and a set of pairwise relationships between them, each with a value representing its neediness, importance, or emotional weight. Find a periodic schedule of pairwise meetings between couples that minimizes the maximal weighted waiting time between such meetings, given that each person can meet with at most one of their partners on any particular day. 
