Step 0 has ruled out the naïve “any planted periodic schedule” justification: the paper explicitly gives an exponential configuration-graph algorithm, polynomial approximations, and an exact polynomial edge-colouring route in important special cases. The promising native family is the paper’s Proposition 1 equivalence between unweighted optimal schedules and edge colourings; I’m now testing whether its construction is honestly Track B (generic colouring is mechanical, while a planted algebraic factorisation is compact) or whether the compact certificate becomes too easy and must be rejected.
