+nonzero; the d matchings partition all edges.  Cycling through them gives a
+period-d schedule meeting every frequency-d deadline.  Generation therefore
+knows the symbolic schedule by inverse generation.  The verifier independently
+expands the rule, checks that it covers exactly the emitted edges, checks every
+day is a matching, and checks the recurrence bound.  It never reads answer.
+
+Easy and mechanical routes.  Misra--Gries gives a polynomial (Delta+1)-edge
+colouring for general graphs, and regular bipartite graphs admit exact Delta
+edge colourings by repeated perfect matching extraction.  For the certificate
+language used here, a direct exhaustive algorithm derives the offset set from
+one row for each of q-1 slopes and compares rows until one works.  Its measured
