+
+## Caveats
+
+- The absent successful oracle run is decisive: local gates establish generation and verification, not no-tool model hardness. The designated shipping rung must remain provisional until the four-vendor harness runs.
+- This is a deliberately structured Track B distribution. Python solves it quickly, and it provides no average-case or cryptographic hardness evidence. The paper's worst-case NP-hardness does not transfer to it.
+- G4 is uniform over the exact declared affine-rule language. It does not model a solver that spots part of the affine structure; G6 and the intended-route measurement address only a few such priors.
+- The generator excludes the first 16 slopes and presentation-alignments used by its audited heuristics. This hardening could itself create a detectable prior; no learned classifier attack was run.
+- General ILP/CP-SAT, SAT encodings, and external algebra systems were not run. They are expected to succeed and belong with the disclosed reference algorithms, not among failing attacks.
+- The symbolic coordinate labels are part of the task. `canonical_key` covers row/neighbour/panel/day permutations, independent affine coordinate changes, side swaps, and compositions; it is not a canonical labelling algorithm for arbitrary unlabeled bipartite graphs.
+- The module needs no `gvlib` feature and remains standard-library-only.
