+## Problem and trust model
 
-The source is Gąsieniec, Smith, and Wild, [*Polyamorous Scheduling*](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.00465). Section 1.1 defines a decision polycule as a frequency-labelled graph: every day's relationships must be a matching, and every relationship of frequency `f` must occur in every `f`-day window. Section 5, Proposition 5.1 proves that an unweighted heat-`d` schedule is exactly a proper `d`-edge-colouring; Lemma 2.1 gives the equivalent frequency-`d` decision schedule used here.
